7D7AF][/dim]adopt heavier epic landers and lighter research swarm members.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]weighted_queue_capacity.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/weighted_queue_capacity.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-z4[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-z4/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Define weighted queue contracts and shared capacity policy in [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]Rust[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-contracts[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-contracts: implement the validated weight value, queue and launch [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire changes, deterministic capacity projection and admission policy, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]editor metadata, and PyO3 contracts.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Preserve weight through prompt editing and durable launch [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]metadata[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]launch-plumbing[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-contracts[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]launch-plumbing: add temporary beta rollout scaffolding and preserve [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]authored and effective weight through directive adapters, launch paths, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]metadata, scan adapters, family continuation inputs, and prompt [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rewrites.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Enforce weighted claims through admission, handoffs, and [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]cleanup[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]admission-lifecycle[dim] · [dim][/dim]after launch-plumbing[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]admission-lifecycle: connect Rust capacity policy to the locked runner [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate and implement family claim transfer, released-family reacquisition,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor and gate handling, and concurrent lifecycle regression coverage.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Separate capacity from counts and render quiet weight badges[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capacity-ux[dim] · [dim][/dim]after admission-lifecycle[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capacity-ux: feed shared capacity into the TUI and CLI, render global [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]usage before status brackets, add non-default agent weight badges and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]queue explanations, and verify refresh and visual behavior.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Adopt workload weights and complete the coordinated rollout[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]presets-rollout[dim] · [dim][/dim]after capacity-ux[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]presets-rollout: apply 2.0 to bundled epic landers and 0.25 to all four [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]research swarm segments, update documentation and package compatibility,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exercise the integrated feature, and remove temporary rollout [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scaffolding.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-z4","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-z4.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e541278113d5d8bb6094749eb2f6246d","started_at":"2026-09-10T00:54:30.649301+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable